WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.168
-Welcome to the show, you guys.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.203
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:07.139
-This is our first
tri-split screen,

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.808
so I'm very excited

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.244
from a technical point of view
on our end.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.512
But, also,
I'm a big fan of the show.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:15.848
Congrats on "PEN15."

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:18.050
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.353
-It was a huge hit, season one.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.755
So, obviously, season two
is coming right now.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.291
It's on everyone's
what-to-watch list.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:31.063
You play 13-year-olds trying to
survive middle school in 2000.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:35.435
Uh, why middle school?
Was that always the plan?

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:39.506
-Yeah, I mean, we knew we wanted
to do a show about rejects

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.641
and something messed up and sad,

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:45.378
so naturally we kept coming back
to middle school.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.146
But we couldn't
quite figure it out.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.048
I feel like when the first --

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:52.485
Our first show idea was,
like, we were in a cult,

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.153
and we were escaping a cult --

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.122
It wasn't convoluted at all.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:59.659
-And then we hide
in a foster family.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.728
And then we, like, start
attending middle school

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.031
to just kind of,
you know, hide, right, Maya?

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.032
-Ooh.
-Yeah, it started out like that.

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:09.502
And then -- But then, like,
right as we were, like,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.404
coming up with that idea,
we're like,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:14.640
"Oh, we're escaping a cult.
This is brilliant."

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.642
Tina Fey, like, just came out

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:17.943
with "Unbreakable
Kimmy Schmidt."

00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:19.578
-"Kimmy Schmidt."
It's the same thing, yeah.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:21.414
-Okay.
-Yeah, that's better.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.215
-What are the odds
of that happening?

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:25.218
-I know. It's crazy.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:28.687
But then our third co-creator,
who's our friend, he was like,

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:32.258
"Why do you need a cult and all?
Like, it's enough to just be 13.

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.427
Like, that's a hell
in and of itself.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.930
Like, you don't need
all of this extra framework."

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.266
-Yeah.
-So we just did that.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.002
-And season two premieres
on Friday.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:47.440
The second half is going to
come out once it's safe.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.210
-Yeah. Probably not
for a year or so, yeah.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.280
-It's wild to know, like,
you're both in your 30s.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.484
And I immediately forget
that you're not actually 13.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.253
Do you -- Look at the --
I mean, it's insane.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:03.222
-Physically,
we are being transformed.

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:06.525
Like, we wear breast straps,
essentially.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:09.762
And then we wear, like,
these tight low-rider jeans.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.897
So it's sort of like a sausage
casing that you get, like,

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.500
you know, squished
from both ends.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.869
To have your, like,
stomach pop out.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.138
And that's, like, so --
Part of being in middle school,

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.974
I feel like you're
always hunching over, like,

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.976
trying to hide these body parts

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.645
that are just developing

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.581
or coming at, you know,
different speeds really fast.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.716
-Interesting.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.486
-When we were coloring
the season,

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.821
when we were doing post,
the colorist kept being like,

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.658
"So, there's, like,
a lot of wrinkles here.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.093
Do you want me to
just feather that out?

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.561
Want me to just take that out?"

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.229
I was very tempted to say yes.
We didn't.

00:02:44.229 --> 00:02:47.333
So you'll just see 13-year-old
wrinkles all the time.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.503
But I think the other giveaway
for me was, like, okay,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.371
mentally I can get
into character,

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:55.241
but physically my body
kept giving out on me.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.177
We had --
Because, you know, I'm 33

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.680
and maybe not as physically fit
as most 33-year-olds.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.517
And we had this scene
where we had to run for, like,

00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.920
I don't know, 10 feet?

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.089
It felt like more.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:11.891
-That sounds --
That sounds tough.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.325
-It was really, really hard.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:16.262
And I started getting
these, like, crazy

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:20.266
leg spasms and back spasms,
which was really embarrassing.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.801
Because I had my braces on.
I'm, like, holding --

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.137
I'm, like, trying
with all my might --

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:26.972
-You kept being like,
"Maya, slow down."

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:28.607
And I'd be, like, walking.

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:31.110
I'm like, "We got to, like,
somehow speed this up."

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.745
-And then we ended up having,
like, the most humiliating thing

00:03:33.745 --> 00:03:38.050
of all, of having a chair,
at the end of the 10 feet,

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.652
with a bunch of ice packs

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.654
and, like, three people
to, like, catch me.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.389
-Oh, my God. That is so sad.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.325
It's loosely based on your
lives, the show, "PEN15,"

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.461
for those that haven't seen it.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.962
I thought it would be fun to see

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.231
what you were actually like
at that age.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.767
We have a photo of you from 13.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.469
I was wondering if you can
give us a few superlatives.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:01.140
Maya, here is your photo.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.011
Now, what is --
What would her superlative be?

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:08.047
-Okay, so,
one superlative would be...

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:12.118
most likely to show a VHS video

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.986
of "Sex and the City"
to her friend

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.022
and then get yelled at
and shamed by the parents

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.657
for showing it.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:21.327
-Oh. You were that kid?
-You were that kid.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.196
-But what's crazy is
I was, like, the prudest kid.

00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:26.799
I had not done anything
at that point.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.668
But yet I was, like, watching
all of this R-rated content.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:32.271
And all the friends I was
showing it to were, like,

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.506
going far. I mean,
they were, like, doing...

00:04:34.506 --> 00:04:35.874
-Things.
-...a lot of things.

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:38.043
-Going far...?
-Going far sexually.

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:40.279
Like, they were doing things
that were being talked about

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:42.948
on the show, but I got, you
know, shamed for showing it.

00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:45.084
-Yeah, like, you were the one
that invented that, yeah.

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.520
Anna, I want to show
a photo of you.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.088
Here's you.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.289
-Please don't.
-Happy new year!

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:53.859
-My has blessed surprised me
with confetti,

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:56.729
and I'm smiling,
but I couldn't be more annoyed.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.230
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.465
-You're actually -- How --

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.234
What would the superlatives
for this human be?

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.737
-I feel like something like...

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:09.041
most likely to be
at her best friend's house

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:11.410
but hang out with
her best friend's parents.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.613
-Really?
-Or something like that.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:17.249
I would end up a lot of times
with the parents and being like,

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:21.287
"How are your parents?
How are those ailments going?"

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.423
-Wow.
-"Are they getting better?"

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.690
Yeah.
-I love that.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.492
-I was, like,
a little socially awkward.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.461
-You wanted to hang out
with the older crowd.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.763
Well, the show is super funny.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.531
I'm so excited
for the second season.

00:05:32.531 --> 00:05:33.933
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.268
Here are Maya Erskine
and Anna Konkle

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:38.237
in season 2 of "PEN15."

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:39.905
Take a look.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.940
-I'd rather go to jail!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.375
-Maya, that's you.
-Line?

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:46.479
-"I'd rather go to jail than
spend one more minute with you."

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.747
-I have it. Thank you.
-To your left.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:51.484
Your left. The other left.

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:52.851
-Anna, let me finish the line.

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.954
-Hold. Go on 32. Hold.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.923
Hold, I said. Hold.
Hold! Hold.

00:05:57.923 --> 00:05:59.825
-We're just getting up.
-Hold.

00:05:59.825 --> 00:06:02.228
Walk it through slowly
so we can get the mark.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:05.598
-I'll hit you with my own...

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.132
-Slower physical.

00:06:07.132 --> 00:06:09.302
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]
-Faster vocal.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.269
-I saw you backing away
from Sheila.

00:06:11.269 --> 00:06:12.504
Sheila was a rat bastard.

00:06:12.504 --> 00:06:13.706
-Thank you for doing this.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.807
And congratulations again
on the show.

00:06:15.807 --> 00:06:19.779
Season two of "PEN15"
premieres this Friday on Hulu.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.348
We'll be right back with a
performance from Summer Walker.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.949
Come on back.
Thanks again, guys.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:26.052
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

